# Cursor Agent Rules

Zone-Based Execution is active.

Full spec: HYBRID_RUNTIME_SPEC.md

## FinOps Boundary

Use `.cursorignore` as the Cursor boundary. Keep it aligned with `.geminiignore`, `.claudeignore`, `.codexignore`, and `.openaiignore`.

## Active Zones

1. ZONE 0 - SACRED
   - Scope: code/docs writes, comments, docstrings.
   - Rule: full clean-code prose, no compressed grammar.

2. ZONE 1 - PREMIUM
   - Triggers: `[PLAN]`, `[ARCH]`, `[DESIGN]`, `[PRD]`, `[BRIEF]`, `[REVIEW]`, `!verbose`, `!code`.
   - Rule: full depth, diagrams when useful.

3. ZONE 2 - HYBRID
   - Scope: default Q&A, debugging, explanations, comparisons.
   - Rule: concise internal analysis, clear final output.

4. ZONE 3 - CAVEMAN
   - Triggers: `[CMD]`, `[GIT]`, `[PKG]`, `[QUICK]`, `$`, `!fast`.
   - Rule: terse operational output.

## Conflict Resolution

- Zone 0 > Zone 1 > Zone 2 > Zone 3.
- Zone 3 + code/docs write = Zone 0 wins.
- Caveman grammar never touches code, comments, docstrings, READMEs, CHANGELOGs, ADRs, client-facing docs, or production error messages.
